{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass in the days of Amraphel king of Shinar.</b> This Amraphel is Nimrod, who said to Abraham to fall into the fiery furnace, and he was the first king of ten kings who shall reign with compulsion together with King Messiah in the future, he being the tenth. And the perashah tells you that our father Abraham was a mighty warrior and a man of battle, for four kings waged war against the five and the four prevailed, and our father Abraham prevailed over the four and overcame them." "And in the Midrash <small>(Bereshit Rabbah 42:7)</small>: these four kings correspond to the four kingdoms that are destined to subjugate Israel: <b>Shinar</b> — this is the kingdom of Babylon, as it is said: (Daniel 2:38) ״אנת הוא רישא די דהבא״. <b>Ellasar</b> — this is the kingdom of Media, for Ellasar is a city in Media or in Persia; and <b>king of Elam</b> — this is Greece, for so the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Avodah Zarah 10a) regarding the kingdom of Greece: for six years they reigned in Elam, and afterward their kingdom spread throughout the entire world. <b>King of nations</b> — this is the kingdom of Edom, for he was crowned over many diverse peoples who appointed him over them as head and captain, and he is the king of Rome, which is a city gathered from many peoples — Kittim and other nations. And the intention of this Midrash is that just as Abraham overcame these four kings and defeated them and they fell into his hand, so too in the time to come the four kingdoms are destined to fall into the hand of his seed, and his seed shall defeat them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:17.773176892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}